# Build output. `build` is anchored to the root on purpose: a `build` directory elsewhere is source
# (conformance/build holds fixtures, compiler/crates/fortis-mir/src/build holds code).
/build/
# Cargo's build directories, wherever a crate is built (compiler/target, the experimental runtime's target, a
# fixture's native/target); their `incremental/` caches are inside them. A bare `incremental/` pattern is not used:
# benchmarks/incremental is source.
target/
# the built website (website/publish.sh publishes it to the orphan branch `website`)
website/dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.rlib
*.rmeta
# fuzz corpora `fortis test --fuzz` keeps beside a program (X-131)
.fortis/
# agents' git worktrees
.claude/worktrees/
# a spike's run logs, written while it runs; the ones its decision record keeps as evidence are added with
# `git add -f` when the spike closes
spikes/*/run-*.log
spikes/*/workload.log
# SP-12b's preregistration (its README's commands) commits these three as the run's evidence
!spikes/SP-12b/workload.log
!spikes/SP-12b/run-50k.log
!spikes/SP-12b/run-500k.log
